# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESOURCE 9 - THE WEEKEND
#
# `weekend.sc:183`, the weekend dialog's own track.
#
# Original: 3838 ticks = 63.97 s.
# Here:     16 bars at 60 bpm = 64.00 s exactly.
#
# ORIGINAL MUSIC. Written to the ROLE the cue plays, never to its notes.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THIS IS NOT A STING. It was catalogued as one and it is sixty-four seconds -
# longer than every location bed in the game, and more than twenty times the
# length of Bad News. It is a PIECE, and it is written and budgeted as one.
#
# Brief: the week is over and nothing is being decided. The player is reading
# what they did with two days off. It is the only cue in the game that is not
# attached to a transaction - no shop, no counter, no clock - and it should be
# the most relaxed thing in the set.
#
# 60 bpm, C major, and a four-bar cycle that goes round four times with only
# the bell changing. That repetition is the point: sixteen bars of development
# would be a piece of music competing with a screen of text, and nothing here
# asks for attention. It is the slowest cue in the game by ten beats.
#
# Sparse is not the same as thin, which is the lesson the first five beds
# taught: the keys sustain right through, the pad carries the 7th and 9th, and
# the bass holds rather than punctuates. What makes it restful is the TEMPO
# and the harmony, not an absence of sound.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

tempo 60
steps 16
swing 0.06
loop 0
space room

part pad    patch=pad   gain=0.82  pan=-0.24
part keys   patch=keys  gain=0.92  pan=0.14
part bell   patch=bell  gain=0.86  pan=0.32
part bass   patch=bass  gain=0.84  pan=0.00
part drums  kit         gain=0.56  pan=0.00

